Q2. Bitmap Free-Space Management:
  The question requires bitmap initialization, allocation, bitmap update, deallocation, updated bitmap, and insufficient-space handling.
Aim:
  To implement bitmap-based free-space management for allocation and deallocation of disk blocks.
Algorithm:
  * Read the total number of disk blocks.
  * Read the bitmap where 0 represents free and 1 represents allocated.
  * Read the number of blocks required.
  * Search for free blocks and allocate them.
  * Update allocated blocks from 0 to 1.
  * If sufficient free blocks are unavailable, display an error.
  * Display the bitmap after allocation.
  * Read the block number to deallocate.
  * Change the block from 1 to 0.
  * Display the updated bitmap.
C Program:
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int n, i, req, block, count = 0;
    printf("Enter disk size: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);
    int bitmap[n];
    printf("Enter bitmap (0=Free, 1=Allocated): ");
    for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
        scanf("%d", &bitmap[i]);
    printf("Enter file size: ");
    scanf("%d", &req);
    printf("Allocated blocks: ");
    for (i = 0; i < n && count < req; i++) {
        if (bitmap[i] == 0) {
            bitmap[i] = 1;
            printf("%d ", i);
            count++;
        }
    }
    if (count < req)
        printf("\nInsufficient free space!");
    else
        printf("\nAllocation successful.");
    printf("\nBitmap after allocation: ");
    for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
        printf("%d ", bitmap[i]);
    printf("\nEnter block to deallocate: ");
    scanf("%d", &block);
    if (block >= 0 && block < n && bitmap[block] == 1) {
        bitmap[block] = 0;
        printf("Block %d deallocated.", block);
    } else {
        printf("Invalid block.");
    }
    printf("\nBitmap after deallocation: ");
    for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
        printf("%d ", bitmap[i]);
    return 0;
}
